# Build-context hygiene. The Dockerfile runs `COPY . .`, so every file not
# excluded here is baked into an image layer. Those layers are immutable and
# stay readable with `docker save` long after the file is deleted from the
# working tree, which is why this file matters more than it looks.
#
# A note on matching, because it differs from .gitignore in a way that matters
# here. Patterns are relative to the context root, not to the repository root
# at any depth: a plain `logs` matches only ./logs, and reaching a nested one
# needs `**/logs`. So the runtime-state and source-package collisions that
# .gitignore has to be careful about (`logs` vs
# app/modules/security/infrastructure/logs/, `storage/` vs
# app/infrastructure/storage/) are not a hazard here. Leading and trailing
# slashes are disregarded, so `logs`, `/logs/` and `logs/` are all the same.
# `!` re-includes are supported, with the last matching line deciding.

# Secrets. docker-compose.yml loads .env for the db and redis services, so
# this file exists in every working checkout. Copying it would bake the DB
# password, the JWT secrets and the SMTP credentials into the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Virtualenvs. .venv is ~119MB and is built against the host interpreter; the
# image installs its own dependencies from requirements.txt.
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Version control: ~5.6MB of history, including anything ever committed.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.dockerignore

# Build inputs, not runtime artifacts. Excluding them does not stop the build:
# the Dockerfile references them by name, which reads the context directly.
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml

# Bytecode compiled for the host interpreter. PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 stops
# new caches being written, but not stale ones from being copied in. Cache
# patterns are left at any depth on purpose -- a cache is never source.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.so

# Tool caches
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Packaging
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
__pypackages__/

# Runtime state, created by the app as appuser at start-up. Shipping a copy
# from the host is both wrong and a chown cost on a large tree.
logs/
storage/
*.sqlite3
*.db

# Tests and design docs. ci.yml runs pytest from a checkout and never from
# this image, and no module under app/ opens a doc file at run time (the
# references in those files are all in comments and docstrings). The one
# architecture document that a test does check lives under app/, so it stays.
tests/
docs/

# Editors and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db